"]}, "overview": "Melanie Stansbury enters the general election as a clear favorite in this Albuquerque-based district, which leaned Democratic by seven points at the presidential level. She holds the advantages of incumbency and a large financial edge, having raised roughly $1.7 million to about $100,000 for Republican Didi Okpareke, with modest outside support and no recorded opposition spending. A mid-October likely-voter poll put Stansbury at 53 percent, and the Albuquerque Journal reported her leading the race. Prediction markets price her chances near 96 percent.\n\nThe campaign has centered on national themes, with mid-October debates focusing on President Trump's agenda, crime, and the war in Iran. Okpareke has run an active but low-funded campaign, and no expert ratings list the contest as competitive. The available evidence points consistently toward a safe Democratic hold, with the main open question being the size of the winning margin rather than the outcome.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9867, "margin": 19.44}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9859, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.985, "margin": 19.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9862, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9827, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9841, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9855, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9883, "margin": 19.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9876, "margin": 19.6}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9849, "margin": 19.6}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9867, "margin": 19.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9862, "margin": 19.6}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9858, "margin": 19.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9878, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9864, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9873, "margin": 19.6}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9836, "margin": 19.6}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem"